+  "summary": "TinyMCE Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability using media plugin `data-mce-object` serialization",
+  "details": "### Impact\nStored XSS vulnerability in the media plugin. Attackers can inject malicious scripts via elements crafted through the data-mce-object attribute, which are created and executed before sanitization. Impacts users of TinyMCE with the media plugin enabled.\n\n### Patches\nThis vulnerability has been patched in TinyMCE 8.9.3 and TinyMCE 7.9.4 by ensuring that, when using the media plugin, any content created through the data-mce-object attribute is properly sanitized first.\n\n### Workarounds\nNo official workaround available.\n\n### Fix\nTo avoid this vulnerability:\n\nUpgrade to TinyMCE 8.9.3 or higher.\nUpgrade to TinyMCE 7.9.4 or higher.\n\n### Acknowledgements\nTiny thanks [Fariskhi Vidyan](https://github.com/farisv) and David Vieira Kurz (HiSolutions AG) for their help identifying this vulnerability.",
